<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<XMLBIBLE version="2.0.1.18" biblename="King James 2000" type="x-bible">
  <BIBLEBOOK bnumber="28">
    <CHAPTER cnumber="5">
      <VERS vnumber="1">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">Hear you this, O priests; and hearken, you house of Israel; and give you ear, O house of the king; for judgment is for you, because you have been a snare on Mizpah, and a net spread upon Tabor.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="2">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">And the revolters are deeply involved in slaughter, though I have been a rebuker of them all.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="3">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">I know Ephraim, and Israel is not hid from me: for now, O Ephraim, you commit harlotry, and Israel is defiled.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="4">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">They will not change their deeds to turn unto their God: for the spirit of harlotry is in the midst of them, and they have not known the LORD.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="5">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">And the pride of Israel does testify to his face: therefore shall Israel and Ephraim fall in their iniquity; Judah also shall fall with them.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="6">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">They shall go with their flocks and with their herds to seek the LORD; but they shall not find him; he has withdrawn himself from them.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="7">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">They have dealt treacherously against the LORD: for they have begotten pagan children: now a new moon shall devour them with their heritage.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="8">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">Blow the horn in Gibeah, and the trumpet in Ramah: cry aloud at Bethaven, beware, O Benjamin.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="9">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">Ephraim shall be desolate in the day of rebuke: among the tribes of Israel have I made known that which shall surely be.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="10">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">The princes of Judah were like them that remove the landmark: therefore I will pour out my wrath upon them like water.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="11">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">Ephraim is oppressed and broken in judgment, because he willingly walked after a human commandment.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="12">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">Therefore will I be unto Ephraim like a moth, and to the house of Judah like rottenness.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="13">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">When Ephraim saw his sickness, and Judah saw his wound, then went Ephraim to the Assyrian, and sent to king Jareb: yet could he not heal you, nor cure you of your wound.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="14">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">For I will be unto Ephraim as a lion, and as a young lion to the house of Judah: I, even I, will tear them and go away; I will take them away, and none shall rescue him.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="15">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">I will go and return to my place, till they acknowledge their offence, and seek my face: in their affliction they will seek me early.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
    </CHAPTER>
  </BIBLEBOOK>
</XMLBIBLE>